B.Hk=new A.n2(B.B9,"EduTrack","A Python-powered School Management System with role-based access, attendance tracking, grading, and complaint management.","\ud83c\udf93 EduTrack \u2014 School Management System\nEduTrack is a comprehensive and user-friendly School Management System built with Python and a graphical user interface (Tkinter). It is designed to streamline and enhance administrative tasks within educational institutions by providing role-based access for Admins, Teachers, and Students.\n\n\u2728 Key Features\n\ud83d\udce5 Admissions & Removal \u2013 Effortlessly admit new students/teachers and remove them when necessary.\n\ud83d\udcca Attendance Tracking \u2013 Teachers can record attendance, while students can access their records.\n\ud83d\udce2 Complaint System \u2013 Students can submit complaints and concerns directly through the interface.\n\ud83d\udcdd Grading & Result Calculation \u2013 Teachers can enter grades, and EduTrack auto-calculates results for students to view, download, or print.\n\ud83d\udcda Notes Management \u2013 Teachers can upload subject notes, and students can easily download or print them.\n\n\ud83d\ude80 Getting Started\n1. Clone the repository: git clone https://github.com/ManojMaurya207/EduTrack.git\n2. Install dependencies: pip install -r requirements.txt\n3. Launch the app: python main.py\n4. Access the system as Admin, Teacher, or Student.\n\n\ud83e\udd1d Contributing\nWe welcome contributions to enhance and expand EduTrack. Steps to contribute:\n- Fork the repository\n- Create a new feature branch\n- Implement your feature or fix\n- Commit and push your changes\n- Submit a pull request\n\n\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Tech Stack\n- Python\n- Tkinter (GUI)\n- SQL Database (CRUD operations, authentication)\n\n\ud83d\udcc8 Highlights\n- Role-based access for Admin, Teacher, and Student users\n- Secure database integration for data storage\n- CRUD operations for managing students, teachers, and academic data\n- Performance visualization & reporting for actionable academic insights.",B.D2,"https://github.com/ManojMaurya207/EduTrack","assets/projects/edutrack.png")
B.Ba=new A.ex(57792,"MaterialIcons",!1)
